Package: zephyr
Architecture: all
Depends:
    python3,
    ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
    bash-completion
Description: Multi-language CLI project templates and helper tools
 zephyr ships language templates for small command-line utilities under
 /usr/share/zephyr/<lang>/ (bash, c, clib, cpp, cpplib, csharp, erlang, go, haskell, java,
 perl, python, ruby, rust, smalltalk, swift, typescript), plus cmdline tools
 (zfr, zfr-create, zfr-rename, zfr-add, zfr-remove, zfr-about,
 zfr-version, zfr-lint, zfr-dist, zfr-ize) to create projects, manage puffs
 (example apps), validate packaging against zephyr style, build source
 tarballs, and upgrade existing trees (`zfr ize`). Instantiated projects are
 expected to call zfr on PATH; zfr is not a create/rename magic token
 (the template placeholder remains zephyr).
